   "source": [
    "# Preserve unmatched records for the professor's validation checks.\n",
    "unmatched = located.loc[located[\"match_status\"] == \"unmatched\"].copy()\n",
    "unmatched.to_csv(\"data/processed/unmatched_housing_records.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "located.to_csv(\"data/processed/housing_production_located_recovered.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "location_summary = located.groupby(\"location_source\")[\"Net Units Completed\"].agg([\"count\", \"sum\"])\n",
    "location_summary.to_csv(\"data/processed/location_source_summary.csv\")\n",
    "location_summary"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4834d3d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a id=\"step-3\"></a>\n",
    "## Step 3 — Assign located housing records to census tracts\n",
    "\n",
    "Use `Point` and `gpd.sjoin()` to place each housing record inside a 2020 Census Tract. **The spatial join is based on coordinates; unmatched rows remain in `detailed` but have no GEOID.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the source's unique `source_row_id` to merge the GEOID back (not `BPA`, which might be repeated). Report the fraction of records and **net housing units** that remain unassigned. This is essential because we simplified Step 2c; do **not** describe the output as a complete citywide map when records lack a tract."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "721a1ae2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
