  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2833a710",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a id=\"step-6\"></a>\n",
    "## Step 6 — Classify tracts using ACS 2020–2024 \n",
    "\n",
    "clean B25003, clean B19013, merge by GEOID, then use `pd.qcut()` to divide tracts into three income groups and three renter-share groups. We use the **same ACS 2024 five-year data** already in this project's `data/raw` folder, so no extra copies or folder changes are needed. The groups describe **2020–2024 conditions**, not neighborhood conditions in 2005.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitation:** Income and renter-share groups reflect 2020–2024 ACS conditions. Neighborhood characteristics may have changed during 2005–2025. The comparisons describe historical housing production grouped by recent neighborhood conditions; they do not establish the income or renter share at the time housing was completed.\n"
   ]
  },
